            "body": "## Code Review\n\nThis pull request correctly addresses an `asyncio` event loop initialization issue for Python 3.10+ compatibility by replacing the deprecated `get_event_loop()` with the recommended `get_running_loop()` pattern. While the core fix is good, the PR also introduces environment variable modifications at the module level. This is a poor practice as it creates global side effects and makes the code harder to maintain and debug. My review includes a comment to address this by suggesting moving the configuration to a more appropriate place, such as the application's entry point. Additionally, these changes are unrelated to the main goal of the PR, and should ideally be in a separate pull request.",
            "comments": {
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "author": {
                    "__typename": "Bot",
                    "login": "gemini-code-assist"
                  },
                  "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nSetting environment variables at the module level introduces global side effects, making system behavior hard to debug. This is considered a poor practice. It's recommended to handle such configurations at the application's entry point or through a dedicated configuration system.\n\nAdditionally, this change seems unrelated to the PR's main goal of fixing event loop compatibility. Please move this to a separate PR or explain its relevance in the description.\n\nFinally, the hardcoded values `536870912` and `0` should be defined as named constants for better readability and maintainability.",
                  "createdAt": "2026-01-15T13:54:46Z",
                  "databaseId": 2694487942,
