  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nSetting environment variables at the module level introduces global side effects, making system behavior hard to debug. This is considered a poor practice. It's recommended to handle such configurations at the application's entry point or through a dedicated configuration system.\n\nAdditionally, this change seems unrelated to the PR's main goal of fixing event loop compatibility. Please move this to a separate PR or explain its relevance in the description.\n\nFinally, the hardcoded values `536870912` and `0` should be defined as named constants for better readability and maintainability.",
      "created_at": "2026-01-15T13:54:46Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -25,10 +25,13 @@\n - Do inference in tp. pp is treated as additional dp\n - After inference, all the parameters that doesn't belong to this pp rank is freed.\n \"\"\"\n-\n+import asyncio\n import getpass\n import logging\n import os\n+\n+os.environ[\"VLLM_FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BUFFER_SIZE\"] = \"536870912\"\n+os.environ[\"VLLM_ALLREDUCE_USE_SYMM_MEM\"] = \"0\"",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pull/4939#discussion_r2694487942",
      "id": 2694487942,
      "line": null,
      "original_line": 34,
