    {
      "body": "Actually, the get_event_loop function does precisely this.",
      "created_at": "2026-01-15T15:42:03Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -160,7 +163,11 @@ def _init_zeromq(self) -> str:\n                     address = f\"tcp://{ip}:{port}\"\n             self.socket.bind(address)\n \n-        loop = get_event_loop()\n+        try:\n+            loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n+        except RuntimeError:\n+            loop = asyncio.new_event_loop()\n+            asyncio.set_event_loop(loop)",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pull/4939#discussion_r2694902212",
      "id": 2694902212,
      "line": 167,
      "original_line": 170,
      "path": "verl/workers/rollout/vllm_rollout/vllm_rollout.py",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-15T15:42:09Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "ji-huazhong"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Thanks for the review!\r\n\r\nActually, this is exactly the error we encountered in production:\r\n```\r\nRuntimeError: no running event loop\r\nFile \"vllm_rollout_spmd.py\", line 575, in _init_zeromq\r\n    loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Root cause**: When using `mode: sync` for PRIME training, Ray workers don't have an async context by default. The ZeroMQ initialization expects to run inside an async context.\r\n\r\nThe existing `get_event_loop()` helper didn't handle this case — we got `RuntimeError: no running event loop` until we added the try/except fallback.\r\n\r\nOur fix:\r\n```python\r\ntry:\r\n    loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\r\nexcept RuntimeError:\r\n    loop = asyncio.new_event_loop()\r\n    asyncio.set_event_loop(loop)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis creates a new event loop when none exists (sync mode), which resolved the issue.\r\n\r\nTested on Python 3.10+ with PRIME training in sync mode — works correctly now.",
      "created_at": "2026-01-15T17:41:31Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -160,7 +163,11 @@ def _init_zeromq(self) -> str:\n                     address = f\"tcp://{ip}:{port}\"\n             self.socket.bind(address)\n \n-        loop = get_event_loop()\n+        try:\n+            loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n+        except RuntimeError:\n+            loop = asyncio.new_event_loop()\n+            asyncio.set_event_loop(loop)",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pull/4939#discussion_r2695353793",
      "id": 2695353793,
      "line": 167,
      "original_line": 170,
      "path": "verl/workers/rollout/vllm_rollout/vllm_rollout.py",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-15T17:41:31Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "KradThed"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "You're right, thanks for catching this! \r\n\r\nRemoved the environment variables — they were accidentally included and are unrelated to the event loop fix. These are B200-specific optimizations that should be handled at the application level.\r\n\r\nPR now focuses only on the Python 3.10+ event loop compatibility fix.",
      "created_at": "2026-01-15T17:44:56Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -25,10 +25,13 @@\n - Do inference in tp. pp is treated as additional dp\n - After inference, all the parameters that doesn't belong to this pp rank is freed.\n \"\"\"\n-\n+import asyncio\n import getpass\n import logging\n import os\n+\n+os.environ[\"VLLM_FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BUFFER_SIZE\"] = \"536870912\"\n+os.environ[\"VLLM_ALLREDUCE_USE_SYMM_MEM\"] = \"0\"",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pull/4939#discussion_r2695367961",
