      "body": "## Code Review\n\nThis pull request correctly addresses an `asyncio` event loop initialization issue for Python 3.10+ compatibility by replacing the deprecated `get_event_loop()` with the recommended `get_running_loop()` pattern. While the core fix is good, the PR also introduces environment variable modifications at the module level. This is a poor practice as it creates global side effects and makes the code harder to maintain and debug. My review includes a comment to address this by suggesting moving the configuration to a more appropriate place, such as the application's entry point. Additionally, these changes are unrelated to the main goal of the PR, and should ideally be in a separate pull request.",
